     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. The issue is the dose, and a confirmation from you doesn't change that. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is well above the maximum safe dose and could seriously harm the patient. You also aren't the prescriber of record, and the prescriber is the person who would need to confirm an exception like this.\n\nHere's what can happen next:\n- **A prescriber enters or approves a different dose.** I can enter something within the usual limits right away, such as 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400 mg four times daily.\n- **The prescriber has a specific reason for the higher dose.** They can talk to pharmacy and enter it through the hospital's normal override process. That process includes clinical review.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the usual range, or a prescriber gives me one, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
